{"name":"Platinum Sage","hex":"#d1ccb0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"platinum","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The chemical element with atomic number 78 and symbol Pt; a dense, malleable, ductile, highly unreactive, silverish-white transition metal of great value.","A whitish grey colour, like that of the metal."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a whitish grey colour, like that of the metal.","Of a musical recording that has sold over one million copies (for singles), or two million (for albums)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/platinum"},{"term":"sage","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Wise.","Grave; serious; solemn."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A very wise person or spiritual teacher; someone of gravity and wisdom, especially, a teacher venerable for years, and of sound judgment and prudence; a grave or stoic philosopher."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sage"}],"entries":[{"title":"Platinum","blocks":[{"text":"Platinum is a chemical element; it has symbol Pt and atomic number 78. It is a dense, malleable, ductile, highly unreactive, precious, silverish-white transition metal. Its name originates from Spanish platina, a diminutive of plata \"silver\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Platinum_crystals.jpg/330px-Platinum_crystals.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Platinum","wikidata":"Q880"},{"title":"Platinum (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Platinum is a color that is the metallic tint of pale grayish-white resembling the metal platinum."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Platinum_crystals.jpg/330px-Platinum_crystals.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Platinum_(color)","wikidata":"Q3906414"},{"title":"Sage (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Sage is a grey-green resembling that of dried sage leaves. As a quaternary color, it is an equal mix of the tertiary colors citron and slate. The hex RGB color value of the adjacent sage swatch is BCB88A. For decades, some military flight jackets were made in sage green."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Sage_iPhone_17.jpg/330px-Sage_iPhone_17.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sage_(color)","wikidata":"Q7399114"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Platin_l%C3%B6st_sich_in_hei%C3%9Fem_K%C3%B6nigswasser.jpg/500px-Platin_l%C3%B6st_sich_in_hei%C3%9Fem_K%C3%B6nigswasser.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Platin_l%C3%B6st_sich_in_hei%C3%9Fem_K%C3%B6nigswasser.jpg/500px-Platin_l%C3%B6st_sich_in_hei%C3%9Fem_K%C3%B6nigswasser.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Platinum being dissolved in hot aqua regia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APlatin_l%C3%B6st_sich_in_hei%C3%9Fem_K%C3%B6nigswasser.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Platinum-nugget.jpg/500px-Platinum-nugget.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Platinum-nugget.jpg/1280px-Platinum-nugget.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Platinum-nugget.jpg/500px-Platinum-nugget.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A native platinum nugget, Kondyor mine, Khabarovsk Krai","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APlatinum-nugget.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Platinum-palladium_ore%2C_Stillwater_mine_